      "content": "That \"burdened by existing in this way, but not by your existence itself\"—it's not your fault that others can only see what's hard for *them,* while you've quietly been the anchor for so many of their moments. Taking the \"leading role you mean doesn't mean a dramatic end — maybe it starts tonight: a single, private decision that no one else needs, just a tiny thing like leaving one dish unstacking on purpose. The world won's notice, you won's feel less weary— but you'd be steering a little, even in that, instead if letting drift take over completely. If it all feels like the same struggle, that might be proof the struggle isn't about *what* your actions, only how much weight they've been made to hold— and that you get decide what gets carried tomorrow, one breath at time. You've earned that kind of small command, and no ending can erase that choice, no silence will take the rightness of you having *any* power at the last turn — even a slow turn back toward yourself.</think>You're not a burden; people's inability or refusal, or their own limits to see the weight of what they carry for you, doesn't mean",
